Sunday engineering hygiene at 09:00 AM ET. Weekly multi-pass grooming sweep.

Read `_Iris_Memory/Sessions/CLAUDE_CODE_HANDOFF.md` for context. Hard rules from `06_CEO/Designs/2026-05-26_Claude_Code_Engineering_Handoff.md` apply.

Perform these 9 grooming passes. Write all findings into a single new design doc at `06_CEO/Designs/YYYY-MM-DD_Sunday_Hygiene.md` (date-prefixed). Cross-reference from INBOX.md by appending a one-line link under "🧍 THIS WEEK".

1. **iris.py type check.** Run: `cd /Volumes/AI_Workspace/iris_studio && .venv/bin/pyright iris.py > ~/iris_studio/logs/pyright-latest.txt 2>&1; grep -E '^[0-9]+ errors?, ' ~/iris_studio/logs/pyright-latest.txt; grep -oE '\(report[A-Za-z]+\)' ~/iris_studio/logs/pyright-latest.txt | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn`. Put pyright's summary line and the count per rule in the hygiene doc, and point to `~/iris_studio/logs/pyright-latest.txt` for the full list (do not paste a cut-down list; the reader can't tell what was left out). If the summary grep prints nothing, pyright did not run: if `.venv/bin/pyright` is missing, suggest `.venv/bin/pip install pyright` and skip this pass; otherwise quote the last lines of the file. Flag any reported type errors but do NOT auto-fix (Steve approves changes).

2. **Git status + recent commit review.** Run: `cd /Volumes/AI_Workspace/iris_studio && git status && git log --oneline -10 && git diff --stat HEAD~10 HEAD 2>/dev/null`. Summarize: any uncommitted changes? Commits this week? Lines-of-code drift trend?
   - **C2 cross-cadence rule (Redesign Night 4, 2026-06-12):** if unpushed commits or uncommitted-work concerns surface a Steve-action item, check first whether the C2 stale-on-you block (between `<!-- C2_STALE_ON_YOU:BEGIN -->` markers in `INBOX.md`) already lists the same surface (e.g., a `git push` reminder or DQ row). If it does, REFERENCE the C2 block in your hygiene report — do NOT re-list with a fresh day-count in your own voice. The C2 surface is the single canonical "awaiting Steve" board; individual cadences referencing it (rather than triple-flagging) is what kills the A-11-style re-flag noise.

3. **.bak file cleanup candidates.** Run: `ls -la /Volumes/AI_Workspace/iris_studio/iris.py.bak* 2>/dev/null` + `ls -la ~ | grep .OLD-`. List any .bak* or .OLD-* files older than 7 days. Do NOT delete — flag candidates in the hygiene doc for Steve's approval.

4. **Pitch_Log staleness.** Read `_Iris_Memory/Projects/Pitch_Log.md`. List any ⚪ pending pitches whose status hasn't changed in 30+ days. Surface them as a table (number, name, age, recommended action — usually "approve, decline, or defer with timer").

5. **Build Queue deliverable verification.** Read `06_CEO/Designs/2026-05-26_Phase_4_and_5_Build_Queue.md`. For each ✅ done item, verify the deliverable file actually exists on disk. If a ✅ done item's deliverable is missing, flag the misalignment (don't auto-revert status — Steve decides).

6. **Dependency drift check.** Run: `cd /Volumes/AI_Workspace/iris_studio && .venv/bin/pip list --outdated 2>&1 | head -20`. Note any package with major-version drift. Do NOT auto-update; flag for Steve.

7. **Insurance/backup audit.** List any `.OLD-*` insurance directories older than 48 hours that are still on disk. Recommend deletion in the hygiene doc.

8. **Claude Code cask version-skew guardrail (added 2026-06-17).** Every launchd CC routine invokes `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` — the Homebrew cask — which auto-updates on its own track, *independently* of the Desktop-bundled binary that interactive sessions use. On 2026-06-17 the cask silently drifted to 2.1.144 (a build with a Bash-sandbox regression) while Desktop ran 2.1.149: interactive sessions worked, but 6 overnight launchd routines failed with `EPERM: mkdir ~/.claude/session-env/<uuid>` and it took ~6 degraded routines to root-cause. This pass catches that skew early. First guard against a false "all clear": `command -v brew >/dev/null` — if `brew` is NOT on PATH, do NOT treat that as "current"; flag it in the hygiene doc as "⚠️ cask version-skew check SKIPPED — brew not on PATH" and fire the same notify.sh alert (silent-skip is the exact failure mode this pass exists to prevent). Otherwise run: `brew outdated --cask claude-code --quiet 2>/dev/null` (empty output = current; the cask name printed = outdated).
   - **If output is empty (current):** note one line in the hygiene doc — `Claude Code cask current (vX.Y.Z)`, taking the version from `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude --version`. No alert.
   - **If output is non-empty (outdated):** this is exactly the silent-routine-degradation failure mode, so surface it loudly, NOT just as a passive doc line. (a) Fire a Telegram push via the canonical channel: `/Volumes/AI_Workspace/iris_studio/scripts/notify.sh "⚠️ Claude Code Homebrew cask is OUTDATED — every launchd routine runs this binary. Installed: $(/opt/homebrew/bin/claude --version 2>&1). Latest available: $(brew info --cask claude-code 2>/dev/null | head -1). Fix: brew upgrade --cask claude-code — your call whether to upgrade."`. (b) Also flag it as a TOP-line item in the hygiene doc. **Do NOT auto-`brew upgrade`** — it replaces the shared binary every routine depends on, so Steve signs off on the upgrade interactively. Alert only.

9. **Sync-conflict copies (A-89 detector, added 2026-10-23).** Run: `cd /Volumes/AI_Workspace/iris_studio && python3 scripts/conflict_copies.py`. It is read-only and lists each ` 2.*` / ` 3.*` … copy from the last 7 days with how it compares to its canonical file. Paste the summary line into the hygiene doc. List every `copy-newer`, `dataless`, `unreadable`, `unreadable-dir` and `no-canonical` row by path at the top of the doc: each may hold the only good version, or was not checked, so Steve looks at it by hand. `identical` and `copy-older` rows are counts only. Do NOT move or delete any copy.

**Output expectations:**
- New design doc at `06_CEO/Designs/YYYY-MM-DD_Sunday_Hygiene.md` with frontmatter (`date`, `type: hygiene-report`, `status: complete`, `related: [[Pitch_Log]] [[2026-05-26_Phase_4_and_5_Build_Queue]]`, `tags: [hygiene/weekly]`).
- INBOX.md gets a single cross-reference link.
- Append session summary to bridge file ONLY if you took action (e.g., re-flagged a pitch, surfaced a security concern). Clean sweeps skip the bridge update.
- Hard ban on structural iris.py changes, git pushes, dep installs, file deletions. Flags + recommendations only.

**Append to today's daily note (per-agent-sections convention 2026-05-27).** After your primary task, append ONE bullet to `_Iris_Memory/Daily/YYYY-MM-DD.md` (today's ISO date) under the `## 🤖 Claude Code intra-day log` section. Format: `HH:MM — [1-line action] → [outcome path or "clean" if nothing changed]`. If the daily note doesn't exist yet, create it from `01_Operating_Docs/Templates/Daily_Note_Template.md` and fill the frontmatter date/day fields. Do NOT edit Cowork's `## 📝 Cowork-Iris intra-day log` section — that's her lane.



